# Winify configuration -- for development only.
#
# Normally Winify asks for your Spotify Client ID on its sign-in screen
# ("Connect your Spotify app") and stores it in its own settings. A Client ID
# here (or in the SPOTIFY_CLIENT_ID environment variable) is used only when
# none has been saved there.
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env` is gitignored and must never be committed.
#
# To get a Client ID, see "Setup" in README.md: create an app at
# https://developer.spotify.com/dashboard, add this Redirect URI exactly,
#     http://127.0.0.1:8888/callback
# tick Web API and Web Playback SDK, and copy the app's Client ID below.
#
# Winify uses the Authorization Code flow with PKCE, so no Client Secret is
# needed. Don't put one here.

SPOTIFY_CLIENT_ID=
